virology-tutorial-name = Virology: outbreak
virology-tutorial-tooltip = Learn to take a swab, grow a culture, find the source of an outbreak and produce a vaccine.

virology-tut-welcome-bubble = Welcome to virology! There is a patient in the ward, and you need to make a vaccine.
virology-tut-welcome-chat = A virologist's work is a chain: take a sample from the patient, grow a culture, identify the strain in the lab and produce a vaccine. Start with protection: never enter the ward without it.
virology-tut-welcome-tts = Welcome to virology. There is a patient in the ward and you need to make a vaccine. Let us start with protection.

virology-tut-equip-mask-bubble = Put on the highlighted sterile mask [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-equip-mask-chat = Diseases travel through the air when a patient coughs or sneezes. A sterile mask stops three quarters of the droplets. A mask pulled down to the chin protects nothing.
virology-tut-equip-mask-tts = Put on the highlighted sterile mask. It stops the droplets released by coughing.

virology-tut-equip-gloves-bubble = Put on the highlighted nitrile gloves [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-equip-gloves-chat = Any gloves fully shield your hands from contagion on touch. Ordinary gloves pick it up and carry it onward, nitrile ones do not. That is why these are the ward gloves.
virology-tut-equip-gloves-tts = Put on the highlighted nitrile gloves. Unlike ordinary ones, they do not pick up contagion.

virology-tut-examine-gloves-bubble = Examine the gloves [tutkeybind="ExamineEntity"] and open "Contagion protection".
virology-tut-examine-gloves-chat = Every item has a "Contagion protection" button in its examine window, next to the armor figures. It shows how much the infection risk drops on each route, and for gloves whether they pick contagion up.
virology-tut-examine-gloves-tts = Examine the gloves and open the contagion protection tab. You can check any item this way before entering the ward.

virology-tut-equip-visor-bubble = Put on the highlighted virology visor [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-equip-visor-chat = The visor highlights contaminated items around you. It does not show infected people: you find those with a swab and an analyzer.
virology-tut-equip-visor-tts = Put on the virology visor. It highlights contaminated items but does not show infected people.

virology-tut-reach-ward-bubble = Walk into the ward to the patient.
virology-tut-reach-ward-chat = Your protection is on, so you can enter. Try not to stay in the ward longer than you need to.
virology-tut-reach-ward-tts = Walk into the ward to the patient.

virology-tut-examine-patient-bubble = Examine the patient [tutkeybind="ExamineEntity"].
virology-tut-examine-patient-chat = Always start with an examination. Visible symptoms such as coughing, a rash or a fever hint at what you are dealing with, but only analysis names the exact strain.
virology-tut-examine-patient-tts = Examine the patient. Visible symptoms hint at what you are dealing with.

virology-tut-take-swab-bubble = Pick up the highlighted swab [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-take-swab-chat = A swab collects a sample of the diseases on a patient or an item. It is single use, but after seeding a dish it stays in your hands and still works in the vaccinator.
virology-tut-take-swab-tts = Pick up the highlighted swab. You will collect a sample from the patient with it.

virology-tut-swab-patient-bubble = Use the swab on the patient [tutkeybind="UIClick"] and wait for it to finish.
virology-tut-swab-patient-chat = Hold the swab and click the patient. A swab works on any target, even a healthy one: otherwise a refusal would reveal that they are clean before any analysis.
virology-tut-swab-patient-tts = Use the swab on the patient and wait for the procedure to finish.

virology-tut-spot-source-bubble = The visor highlights a tray. Examine it [tutkeybind="ExamineEntity"].
virology-tut-spot-source-chat = This is what the visor is for: contaminated items glow. While the source sits in the ward it infects everyone who touches it, and the outbreak will not end even if you cure the patient.
virology-tut-spot-source-tts = The visor highlights a contaminated tray. Examine it: this is a source and it has to be treated.

virology-tut-take-sprayer-bubble = Pick up the highlighted sprayer [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-take-sprayer-chat = The sprayer is filled with disinfectant. It clears contagion from items and from the dead, but does nothing for the living: that is what a vaccine is for.
virology-tut-take-sprayer-tts = Pick up the highlighted disinfectant sprayer.

virology-tut-disinfect-bubble = Treat the tray with the sprayer [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-disinfect-chat = Click the tray with the sprayer. A treated item stops being a source and goes dark in the visor. The same trick cleans contaminated gloves without taking them off.
virology-tut-disinfect-tts = Treat the tray with the sprayer. After that it will no longer be a source.

virology-tut-reach-lab-bubble = Walk to the lab through the sterilizer arch.
virology-tut-reach-lab-chat = The arch sprays disinfectant over everything you are wearing and beeps if an infected person walked through. Pass through it every time you leave the ward.
virology-tut-reach-lab-tts = Walk to the lab through the sterilizer arch. It will treat your clothing.

virology-tut-seed-dish-bubble = Seed the highlighted petri dish with the swab [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-seed-dish-chat = Click the dish with the swab. A culture is the second research route beside examining patients: it grows without a patient. If the swab was clean, nothing will grow in the dish.
virology-tut-seed-dish-tts = Seed the petri dish with the swab. A culture of the strain will grow from it.

virology-tut-grow-wait-bubble = The culture is growing. Wait a moment.
virology-tut-grow-wait-chat = On the station a culture takes about a minute, here only a few seconds. While it grows, keep the swab: the vaccinator will need it.
virology-tut-grow-wait-tts = The culture is growing. On the station this takes about a minute.

virology-tut-take-dish-bubble = Pick up the grown culture [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-take-dish-chat = The culture is ready. Feed it to the diagnoser for an exact report on the strain.
virology-tut-take-dish-tts = Pick up the grown culture.

virology-tut-insert-diagnoser-bubble = Insert the culture into the highlighted diagnoser [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-insert-diagnoser-chat = The diagnoser gives an exact analysis: strain code, symptoms, pathogen class and treatment hints. A culture is worth more research points than a swab and reveals one more unnoticed symptom.
virology-tut-insert-diagnoser-tts = Insert the culture into the diagnoser. It will print an exact report on the strain.

virology-tut-read-report-bubble = The diagnoser is printing a report. Feel free to take it and read it.
virology-tut-read-report-chat = The report lists the strain code, its symptoms and the pathogen class. All of it also goes into the station's virus database.
virology-tut-read-report-tts = The diagnoser is printing a report with the strain code, symptoms and pathogen class.

virology-tut-open-database-bubble = Open the highlighted virus database console [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-open-database-chat = The database collects everything the station has learned about strains. Open it and look at your strain's record.
virology-tut-open-database-tts = Open the virus database console.

virology-tut-explain-database-bubble = The record holds everything known about the strain.
virology-tut-explain-database-chat = It shows the strain code, its syndrome, pathogen class, noticed symptoms and research progress. The console dispenses a strain vial every twenty seconds: it cannot infect anyone, but a culture grows from it.
virology-tut-explain-database-tts = The record holds the strain code, class, noticed symptoms and research progress. The console also dispenses vials for seeding dishes.

virology-tut-insert-vaccinator-bubble = Insert the swab into the highlighted vaccinator [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-insert-vaccinator-chat = The vaccinator works out a vaccine from a sample. It needs a swab; a culture does not fit.
virology-tut-insert-vaccinator-tts = Insert the swab into the vaccinator.

virology-tut-open-vaccinator-bubble = Open the vaccinator [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-open-vaccinator-chat = Open the machine window: it lists the trial batches you have to choose from.
virology-tut-open-vaccinator-tts = Open the vaccinator window.

virology-tut-explain-batches-bubble = Pick the batch that matches what you learned about the strain and run it.
virology-tut-explain-batches-chat = Each batch is a set of claims about the strain. The right one is where every claim matches the report: the pathogen class and the symptoms. A miss costs biomass, spends the swab and puts the machine into a flush cycle, so study the strain before guessing. The stronger the strain, the more batches there are and the more locked claims they hold, which research points unlock.
virology-tut-explain-batches-tts = Each batch is a set of claims about the strain. Pick the one that matches the diagnoser report and run it. A miss costs biomass and puts the machine into a flush cycle.

virology-tut-produce-vaccine-bubble = Produce a dose and pick up the vaccine [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-produce-vaccine-chat = The recipe is solved. From now on each dose costs a little biomass and the swab stays in the machine, so you can produce vaccine for the whole department.
virology-tut-produce-vaccine-tts = Produce a dose of the vaccine and pick it up.

virology-tut-inject-patient-bubble = Inject the vaccine into the patient [tutkeybind="UIClick"].
virology-tut-inject-patient-chat = A vaccine starts recovery and grants immunity to that strain. A serum made from a recovered donor's blood only treats the illness and grants no immunity.
virology-tut-inject-patient-tts = Inject the vaccine into the patient. It will cure them and grant immunity to this strain.

virology-tut-finish-bubble = Done! You went through the whole virologist chain.
virology-tut-finish-chat = You took a swab, grew a culture, identified the strain, found the source and produced a vaccine. On the station remember the main thing: find the source, or the outbreak starts over, and keep your protection on. The second tutorial teaches you to design your own strains under the microscope.
virology-tut-finish-tts = Done. You went through the whole chain: swab, culture, analysis, source and vaccine. The second tutorial teaches you to design your own strains.

virology-tut-softlock-keep-swab = Do not drop the swab, you will still need it.
virology-tut-softlock-keep-vaccine = Do not drop the vaccine, the patient needs it.

disease-tutorial-cold-name = training cold
disease-tutorial-cold-description = A harmless lab strain used for training. It does not pass from person to person.
